.TH AISHA 1 "November 2026" "aisha" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aisha \- natural-language shell with a local LLM fallback
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aisha
.br
.B aisha
.I request-or-command
.br
.B aisha \-n
.I request
.br
.B aisha \-c
.I line
.br
.B aisha \-\-setup
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aisha
is an interactive shell that accepts both bash and plain-language requests.
Real commands (a program on PATH with flags, paths, pipes or redirects) run in
bash unchanged.
Other lines go to a deterministic rule engine that builds the command from the
words and prints what it understood on a line starting with \(->.
Only when the rules are not confident is a small local language model asked,
through any OpenAI-compatible server; its command is always shown and
confirmed before it runs, and approved answers are remembered.
.PP
Commands that delete or change data always ask
.B [y/N]
first, and deletes list the matching files before asking.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
find recursively files older than 2 months from this folder
find logs older than 2 months and move them to archive
edit logs.txt
edit logs.txt with micro
show the 5 newest files here
which files mention "invoice"
what's eating my disk
.fi
.SH INSIDE THE SHELL
.TP
.BI ! command
run in bash, skipping the rules
.TP
.BI ? request
skip the rules and ask the LLM
.TP
.BI explain " request"
show what would run, run nothing
.TP
.BR learned ", " forget " \fIrequest\fR"
list or drop remembered LLM answers
.TP
.B llm
check the local model
.TP
.BR exit ", Ctrl-D"
leave
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-n
print the command that would run, and run nothing
.TP
.B \-c
run one line and exit
.TP
.B \-\-setup
set up and check the local LLM fallback
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AISHA_LLM_URL
OpenAI-compatible endpoint (default http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1, Ollama)
.TP
.B AISHA_LLM_MODEL
model name (default qwen2.5-coder:1.5b)
.TP
.B AISHA_LLM
set to off to disable the LLM fallback
.TP
.B AISHA_THRESHOLD
confidence below which the rules defer to the LLM (default 0.7)
.TP
.B AISHA_CONFIRM
llm (default), always, or destructive
.TP
.BR VISUAL ", " EDITOR
editor used by "edit FILE" (through sensible-editor on Debian)
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ai-bash/aisha/config.json
settings (same keys as the environment variables, lower case without AISHA_)
.TP
.I ~/.config/ai-bash/aisha/learned.json
remembered phrases
.TP
.I ~/.config/ai-bash/aisha/history
command history
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1),
.BR find (1),
.BR sensible-editor (1)
